        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ios): make Talk audio lifecycle-safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCancelled or timed-out iOS push-to-talk work could remain queued and later acquire the microphone. Related asynchronous owners—including continuous Talk, realtime relay, Voice Wake, screen/camera audio, Gateway requests, speech playback, and restored session routing—could also outlive the app state, Gateway route, or chat session that created them.\n\nThose races could restart stale capture, deliver a reply into a replacement session, let old cleanup stop a newer owner, or admit Talk before a cold-start routing identity finished restoring.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOnly push-to-talk capture preparation is serialized. Stop and cancel bypass that queue, while capture IDs, command epochs, and a finishing owner keep the microphone lease through transcript, chat, history, and speech completion.\n\nApp foreground state and explicit audio leases now gate every microphone owner. Talk, Voice Wake, realtime relay, ReplayKit capture, Gateway requests, speech tasks, and recognition callbacks use lifecycle generations or route leases so suspended work cannot mutate replacement state. Same-route reconnects preserve and await the pending SQLite routing restore; target switches cancel it and canceled loads cannot apply after suspension.\n\nNo Gateway protocol or public configuration surface changes.\n\n## User Impact\n\nStopping, canceling, backgrounding, changing sessions, reconnecting, or replacing a Gateway can no longer let stale iOS voice work reopen the microphone, play an old reply, or affect the next session. Continuous Talk resumes only from its current owner, Voice Wake suppression follows the real audio owner, and camera/screen microphone capture remains single-owner and cancellation-safe.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact reviewed head: `f19f6bb9c0b16d45faccb985477762e5b0306489`.\n- Deterministic regressions cover queued and active PTT cancellation, finalizer ownership, session and route replacement, background admission, Voice Wake generations, realtime relay stop races, ReplayKit single-flight cleanup, Gateway cancellation, and routing hydration across reconnect/target switch.\n- All 22 changed Swift files parse in DEBUG and Release modes; scoped SwiftFormat reports 0 files requiring formatting.\n- Native i18n check passes with 2,916 entries; every unchanged localization identity retains its prior stable ID.\n- `git diff --check` and the fresh whole-branch autoreview pass.\n- Exact-head public CI and iOS Periphery results will be linked in the pre-land proof comment.\n- Hardware gap: no physical iPhone is attached to this host, so microphone/privacy-indicator timing has deterministic lifecycle coverage and exact public CI, but no physical-device run.\n",
